Notebook[{
Cell["WolframExample: Rust libraries from the Wolfram Language", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"9356ac5b-3bfb-49c9-8f6b-b569bb2eba63"],

Cell["\<\
This notebook exercises the WolframExample paclet, whose functions are \
implemented in Rust (see WolframExample/Libs). Evaluate it top to bottom.

If the setup section reports a missing paclet, build the library first:
    cd WolframExample && cargo wl build\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"66d48baf-6f82-48cf-b1ca-2497c4c3a15f"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Setup", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"7c701fa2-7584-45f7-b105-de0cc60f6ef8"],

Cell["\<\
Both paclets \[LongDash] the hand-written WolframExample and the generated \
WolframExampleLib \[LongDash] sit in this notebook's parent directory, so one \
PacletDirectoryLoad registers both.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"cd64cd2e-3022-408e-b637-739cc136be4e"],

Cell["PacletDirectoryLoad[ParentDirectory[NotebookDirectory[]]]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"1de71538-5273-479a-9e8e-7dae9da36818"],

Cell["PacletObject[\"WolframExample\"]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"54311a74-2a9d-4390-9f49-d8908619b308"],

Cell["\<\
The library paclet holds nothing but the compiled dylibs and a generated \
Functions.wl loader:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"918cc84d-a65a-479a-95e2-c73c68f19ede"],

Cell["PacletObject[\"WolframExampleLib\"]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"b9240851-884f-44ed-9842-87ada29c5a50"],

Cell["Needs[\"WolframExample`\"]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"3243027f-721b-4495-a225-2de62f72a05a"],

Cell["Everything the package exports:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"b678df16-8bb6-474d-ba8e-9a9354c38266"],

Cell["?WolframExample`*", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"203168eb-4817-41da-b12a-76eb43732430"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Math", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"50809788-17be-42cf-92b8-a58d336238bd"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Scalars and arrays", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"72785aaa-6c28-47eb-869f-e3c3b9ad530f"],

Cell["\<\
A plain Rust function over two f64s. Arguments and result cross as raw \
MArgument scalars \[LongDash] no serialization at all.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"564e54dd-45c1-48f3-a62d-1a28ae315326"],

Cell["ExampleAdd[2, 3]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"e614913a-2100-4eef-ac93-e3091cfac593"],

Cell["\<\
NumericArrays are read zero-copy: Rust sees the kernel's own memory, no copy \
and no conversion. Lists are packed into a Real64 NumericArray by the wrapper \
first.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6b7fb325-9f86-4135-b86c-3bfbd0bebc40"],

Cell["ExampleDot[{1, 2, 3}, {4, 5, 6}]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"e3171dbc-93cb-47c4-b729-9e33bf5ce240"],

Cell["\<\
ExampleDot[
    NumericArray[Range[1., 100000.], \"Real64\"],
    NumericArray[Range[100000., 1., -1.], \"Real64\"]
]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"b4c1a79d-7314-45f5-a0f9-19f207418b77"],

Cell["\<\
The Rust side accumulates into 8 independent lanes so that LLVM can vectorize \
the loop (see Libs/math/src/lib.rs) \[LongDash] about twice the throughput of \
the naive left-to-right sum. Timed against the kernel's own Dot, which calls \
into BLAS; a Speedup above 1 means the Rust library won.

Two things decide what you see here. Time only the call, not the packing: \
both arrays are converted to NumericArrays first, since passing plain lists \
spends about three times the call itself on the conversion. And build with    \
 cargo wl build --release
\[LongDash] cargo wl test leaves an unoptimized build in place, which loses \
by an order of magnitude.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"267d9a96-0823-4dc9-9c4e-5e2bd18b48c2"],

Cell["\<\
With[
    {a = Range[1., 100000.], b = Range[100000., 1., -1.]},
    {na = NumericArray[a, \"Real64\"], nb = NumericArray[b, \"Real64\"]},
    {rust = First @ RepeatedTiming @ ExampleDot[na, nb],
     kernel = First @ RepeatedTiming @ Dot[a, b],
     packing = First @ RepeatedTiming @ ExampleDot[a, b]},
    <|
        \"Rust\" -> Quantity[rust, \"Seconds\"],
        \"Kernel\" -> Quantity[kernel, \"Seconds\"],
        \"Speedup\" -> kernel / rust,
        \"RustFromLists\" -> Quantity[packing, \"Seconds\"]
    |>
]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"a314277d-a655-4bfb-ab15-2d3ae4e655c4"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Structs and enums", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"6fb0097d-cb25-41de-a702-2dd8d1a8d31e"],

Cell["\<\
Structured arguments cross as WXF. A Rust struct is an Association keyed by \
its field names; the wrapper here presents Wolfram-style capitalized keys.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7bd5b8a4-e384-4248-86eb-649f83bbfb32"],

Cell["ExampleSymmetricPoint[<|\"X\" -> 10, \"Y\" -> 20|>]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"ba36437b-cc46-4fd6-9ef6-4256e22dc357"],

Cell["\<\
ExampleArea goes through a Rust enum \[LongDash] one function, one match, two \
shapes:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"75406be4-9b88-47f3-807c-1d479ac4202d"],

Cell["ExampleArea[<|\"Radius\" -> 1|>]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"c8eb6d12-f2b7-47c1-b3f0-56a0f45317c2"],

Cell["ExampleArea[<|\"Width\" -> 10, \"Height\" -> 20|>]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"b6706dc9-f07c-437f-8039-d61fb739461f"],

Cell["Table[ExampleArea[<|\"Radius\" -> r|>], {r, 1, 5}]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"f83bc06f-c81a-442e-9094-3acd431c1470"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Errors", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"2a66fe18-d1ac-43ef-bc2c-5aae5a02f33b"],

Cell["\<\
A Rust Result<f64, String> comes back as {\"Ok\", value} or {\"Err\", \
message}; the wrapper turns the error branch into a Failure.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"588f394d-8dba-44d1-80b0-ca69d43def7b"],

Cell["ExampleSafeDivide[10, 4]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"ad8fa19e-828b-4ccf-85e2-9505f9c44aae"],

Cell["ExampleSafeDivide[1, 0]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"bd4bc049-b806-42f3-816b-52582fb01bfd"],

Cell["So the usual Failure handling applies:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"07fa4ec5-d055-4f0a-b011-15c7ca69b3dd"],

Cell["\<\
FailureQ /@ {ExampleSafeDivide[1, 2], ExampleSafeDivide[1, 0]}\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"92ec2438-b669-4b9d-9238-28066c4eb282"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["DuckDB", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"30bdab3b-1e35-43f1-bce6-883c361175fb"],

Cell["\<\
An entire embedded SQL engine, statically linked into the library \[LongDash] \
nothing to install. Query results come back as Arrow and are decoded into a \
Tabular.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"db04d8d4-35c3-42f9-98cb-e71687956e89"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Scoped connections", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"ad79787d-cfca-4a64-857e-5d44ad9c3296"],

Cell["\<\
DuckDBExecute opens a connection, applies the function to it, and closes it \
again \[LongDash] even if the body fails.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"c22630ff-216f-4895-bc45-b9e9a337769d"],

Cell["\<\
DuckDBExecute[\"duckdb://\", DuckDBQuery[#, \"SELECT 42 AS answer\"] &]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"183614e8-f1e0-4672-8c85-ca09ca8bf599"],

Cell["\<\
DuckDBExecute[\"duckdb://\", DuckDBQuery[#,
    \"SELECT n::INTEGER AS id,
            (n * 1.5)::DOUBLE AS score,
            'item_' || n AS label,
            n % 2 = 0 AS is_even
     FROM generate_series(1, 5) t(n)\"] &]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"5a909cf8-d3a4-4678-a5d0-ed67288e35e8"],

Cell["\<\
The result is an ordinary Tabular, so the usual operations work:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"a74c0a2a-3a01-435e-9753-0e0c8a260ee2"],

Cell["\<\
tab = DuckDBExecute[\"duckdb://\", DuckDBQuery[#,
    \"SELECT n FROM generate_series(1, 100) t(n)\"] &];
{Length[tab], Total[tab[[All, \"n\"]]]}\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"ef28b4f7-e3de-4a76-8614-57bddf5f5e39"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Parameters", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"8833dd3f-b2cc-4ed3-9be9-30496fe8ef94"],

Cell["\<\
Values are bound to the ? placeholders in order, so nothing is interpolated \
into the SQL string.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7917de98-05b4-45b5-9e47-81302b3d22eb"],

Cell["\<\
DuckDBExecute[\"duckdb://\", DuckDBQuery[#,
    \"SELECT n FROM generate_series(1, 5) t(n) WHERE n > ?\", {2}] &]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"8694abdb-345c-4c4d-b861-fdd60b93f22a"],

Cell["\<\
DuckDBExecute[\"duckdb://\", DuckDBQuery[#,
    \"SELECT ?::INTEGER + ?::INTEGER AS total\", {20, 22}] &]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"87b91467-d8ba-4e79-b9ad-ec7c23659117"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Explicit connections", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"6bbcd0b9-cd53-4ba6-822e-09833aa83199"],

Cell["\<\
For several statements against the same database, hold the handle yourself. \
Here an on-disk file, which persists after disconnecting.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"48019240-4576-4f76-9828-bbe2246c6a2b"],

Cell["\<\
file = FileNameJoin[{$TemporaryDirectory, \"wolfram-example.duckdb\"}];
Quiet[DeleteFile[file]];
conn = DuckDBConnect[\"duckdb:///\" <> file]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"f585d644-2350-4a96-bbbf-84b9019f06af"],

Cell["\<\
DuckDBQuery[conn,
    \"CREATE TABLE fruit AS SELECT * FROM (VALUES (1, 'apple'), (2, 'pear')) \
v(id, name)\"]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"efdba532-c7c9-48a4-ab69-e846c6110e0e"],

Cell["\<\
DuckDBQuery[conn, \"INSERT INTO fruit VALUES (?, ?)\", {3, \"plum\"}]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"bf2bd1ad-7814-47e6-a9be-4a598829bd34"],

Cell["DuckDBQuery[conn, \"SELECT * FROM fruit ORDER BY id\"]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"5aefd03e-c459-4327-8838-e4049607b39e"],

Cell["DuckDBDisconnect[conn]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"5e06ea08-b527-4585-bfef-67a1dd5ea0d2"],

Cell["Reopening the same file shows the rows are still there:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"cf7f930c-4860-47ac-9686-96322869da7d"],

Cell["\<\
DuckDBExecute[\"duckdb:///\" <> file,
    DuckDBQuery[#, \"SELECT count(*) AS rows FROM fruit\"] &]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"6c26fcd7-2ddf-4569-85de-e2ea76e70344"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Failures", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"d4d1247e-7e27-4cc8-b5e8-83f9636c41b1"],

Cell["\<\
Errors from the engine arrive as Failure objects carrying DuckDB's own \
message, and propagate on their own.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"80f252af-a1e4-4ed3-a210-441c992ec0e2"],

Cell["\<\
DuckDBExecute[\"duckdb://\", DuckDBQuery[#, \"SELECT * FROM no_such_table\"] \
&]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"69e25f87-cd41-4361-a7fb-e52c83c83e93"],

Cell["\<\
A handle that has been closed is no longer in the Rust-side registry:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"1d732747-3c49-4db7-8066-7222759d5f67"],

Cell["\<\
With[{c = DuckDBConnect[]},
    DuckDBDisconnect[c];
    DuckDBQuery[c, \"SELECT 1\"]
]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"e99782c2-ef95-472b-bc84-d93d353b080c"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["The raw library", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"04d9913c-bf41-4f41-b39a-cc05ebd77113"],

Cell["\<\
The wrappers in Kernel/WolframExample.wl are a thin layer over an association \
of LibraryFunctions, keyed \"namespace::rust_name\". Anything without a \
wrapper is still one lookup away.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"a0d98aad-033d-4fcc-8cd2-9528892f6fc3"],

Cell["Keys[WolframExampleFunctions[]]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"ee6f046b-0886-4df6-91e5-caca88dbf8f7"],

Cell["\<\
inactive_sum builds an expression in Rust and returns it unevaluated:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"b0ca1969-c08e-473a-97dd-86d6a7216b00"],

Cell["WolframExampleFunctions[][\"math::inactive_sum\"][{1, 2, 3}]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"8b1ae366-dae3-42a6-907c-0b29462825aa"],

Cell["\<\
Activate[WolframExampleFunctions[][\"math::inactive_sum\"][{1, 2, 3}]]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"dfd06548-eebb-4cd9-98eb-bcb6f5e24d79"],

Cell["\<\
A panic on the Rust side is caught at the boundary and returned as a Failure \
\[LongDash] it does not take the kernel down:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"c12430f0-5515-4d80-ab0e-da98f70e8234"],

Cell["WolframExampleFunctions[][\"math::panic\"][]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"a0494157-5ac6-4a9f-90c8-4390da6cefe5"],

Cell["\<\
And the signatures of everything that was packaged, straight from the \
generated Artifacts.wl asset:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"05aaf418-22c2-4969-b3ec-22d705d6a394"],

Cell["\<\
Get[PacletObject[\"WolframExampleLib\"][\"AssetLocation\", \"Artifacts\"]] //
    Map[Query[{\"Name\", \"Signatures\"}]] // Dataset\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"0565ce7e-79b3-45c1-8340-6f17a058de54"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Licensing", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"7828ce6e-6669-4277-b776-a5e1a9cb8376"],

Cell["\<\
Everything the library links is compiled into the dylib, so the paclet has to \
carry its own attribution. cargo wl build writes that out as a third asset, \
License.wl: one entry per Rust package in the resolved dependency graph, \
dev-dependencies excluded.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"cec8b45b-7f72-4aa5-881d-9be82521578f"],

Cell["\<\
licenses = Get[PacletObject[\"WolframExampleLib\"][\"AssetLocation\", \
\"License\"]];
Length[licenses]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"bc0306c8-ae4f-4b9f-819f-98262b962966"],

Cell["\<\
Each entry carries what the crate's own Cargo.toml declared \[LongDash] \
undeclared fields come back as Missing[\"NotAvailable\"]:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"606fc878-4ad3-4490-8176-38cd1a4c5536"],

Cell["Dataset[Take[licenses, 8]]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"42622d64-ff82-4f40-8cf1-2c0dd6043d96"],

Cell["\<\
Which licenses the paclet actually ships under, most common first. The values \
are SPDX expressions, so an OR means the crate lets you pick:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"bdc793ef-6193-43e0-a4df-a3d4f1853992"],

Cell["ReverseSort[Counts[licenses[[All, \"License\"]]]] // Dataset", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"101294b3-ed62-48db-9a66-d97e6ae78765"],

Cell["\<\
The entries worth a human's attention \[LongDash] anything that declared no \
license at all. Here that is the two example crates themselves: neither \
Libs/math nor Libs/duckdb sets a license field, which a paclet you actually \
shipped would want to fix:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"c72db599-79a8-410e-bfef-84f1a2038477"],

Cell["Select[licenses, MissingQ[#[\"License\"]] &] // Dataset", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"643de8e6-2161-440d-906b-ab39b9db23fa"],

Cell["\<\
And the direct dependencies of the two example crates, as opposed to the \
whole transitive graph:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"106e5fe2-d209-49b8-80e6-9327f2db9edd"],

Cell["\<\
Select[licenses,
    MemberQ[{\"duckdb\", \"arrow-ipc\", \"uuid\", \"wolfram-expr\",
             \"wolfram-export\", \"wolfram-serialize\", \
\"wolfram-library-link\"},
        #[\"Name\"]] &] // Dataset\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"d7938149-082b-435d-9b16-e7a2c1001a1e"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Rebuilding", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"d6893d6f-e394-448a-82f2-3a36700225b1"],

Cell["\<\
After editing the Rust source, rebuild from the paclet directory. The dylibs \
are content-hashed, so a rebuilt library gets a new file name \[LongDash] \
quit the kernel to pick it up.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"136b062b-c489-4739-a3b3-3ec158496401"],

Cell["\<\
ExternalEvaluate[{\"Shell\",
    \"ProcessDirectory\" -> \
FileNameJoin[{ParentDirectory[NotebookDirectory[]], \"WolframExample\"}],
    \"ProcessEnvironment\" -> <|\"PATH\" -> Environment[\"PATH\"]|>},
   \"cargo wl build --release\"]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"83b99184-7d96-4d71-a91f-5d8e5250565f"]
}, Open  ]]
},
WindowTitle->"WolframExample Tour",
FrontEndVersion->"15.0 for Mac OS X ARM (64-bit) (May 6, 2026)",
StyleDefinitions->"Default.nb",
ExpressionUUID->"24e8828a-1a86-4b98-9199-b892bef13359"
]
